# g95-fu-ssh-service wiring (desktop)

## 1. apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts publishWindowFocus: every on-screen session of a window
Replace
    const sessionId = screenSessionIds(window)[0];
    windows.push({
      connectionId,
      visible: window.isVisible() && !window.isMinimized(),
      focused: window.isFocused(),
      ...(sessionId ? { sessionId } : {}),
    });
by
    const sessionIds = screenSessionIds(window);
    windows.push({
      connectionId,
      visible: window.isVisible() && !window.isMinimized(),
      focused: window.isFocused(),
      ...(sessionIds.length > 0 ? { sessionIds } : {}),
    });
(WindowFocusEntry.sessionIds is the protocol type after the rows of g95-fu-ssh-service are applied; sessionId is gone.)

## 2. apps/desktop/src/main/host/notification.ts: host/notification/close
In registerNotificationHost: keep the toasts by connection, and close a connection's when the core says so.
 - `HOST_METHOD.notificationClose = 'host/notification/close'` in host/connection.ts (hot file, next to notificationShow).
 - Beside `live` add `const byConnection = new Map<string, Set<Pick<Notification, 'on' | 'show' | 'close'>>>();`. In the show handler, for a toast with a `connectionId`
   (`server`), add the notification to `byConnection.get(server)` (create the set) and remove it again on its 'close' and 'click' events (delete the key when the set is empty).
   `NotificationPresenter.createNotification` returns `Pick<Notification, 'on' | 'show'>`: add `'close'` to that Pick (Electron's Notification has close()).
 - New handler:
       connection.handleNotification(HOST_METHOD.notificationClose, (params) => {
         const { connectionId } = objectParams<HostNotificationCloseParams>(params, HOST_METHOD.notificationClose);
         if (typeof connectionId !== 'string' || !connectionId) return;
         for (const notification of [...(byConnection.get(connectionId) ?? [])]) notification.close();
         byConnection.delete(connectionId);
       });
   (import HostNotificationCloseParams from packages/protocol after the rows are applied).
 - The host's `serves` list (host/index.ts), if it names methods, names host/notification/close beside host/notification/show.

## 3. Claim resources
Nothing new here: `host/claim` already sends `resources {serverCoresDir, askpassHelper}` from the desktop (g95-fu-desktop-host owns that side); the core now reads them (core .wire section 2).

## 4. remote-hosts.ts
`watchHostListsFeed` is not in this tree (the duplicated section parsing is already gone): nothing to remove.
